Article 6 (Materials to Be Attached to Applications for Permission to Conduct Litigation)
(1) An organization prescribed in subparagraph 1 of Article 51 of the Act shall attach the following materials, etc. to its application for permission to conduct litigation:
1. Its articles of association;
2. Materials substantiating that the organization has at least 1,000 regular members;
3. A document substantiating the fact and date of the organization's registration as a consumer organization under Article 29 of the Framework Act on Consumers.
(2) An organization prescribed in subparagraph 2 of Article 51 of the Act shall attach the following materials, etc. to its application for permission to conduct litigation:
1. Its articles of association;
2. Its record of activities relating to personal information protection during the most recent three years;
3. Materials substantiating that the organization has at least 5,000 standing members;
4. A document substantiating that the organization is registered with a central administrative agency;
5. The names, addresses, and contact details (including telephone numbers, facsimile numbers, or email addresses) of the data subjects who requested the filing of collective litigation;
6. Written requests for the filing of collective litigation made by the data subjects referred to in subparagraph 5 (including details of the infringement suffered by each data subject and that data subject's signature or seal).
(3) An organization filing a lawsuit shall attach to its application for permission to conduct litigation documents proving that a personal information controller refused collective dispute mediation under Article 49 of the Act or did not accept the result of such mediation, pursuant to Article 54 (2) 2 of the Act.
